  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Timothy T. Coates (Petitioners)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6ab8ec21006ec8570d912efa69199859f3cbda0c74cea37ba4b0609d14a02c90",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6ab8ec21006e-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Timothy T. Coates (Petitioners), petitioners argue that the Ninth Circuit\u2019s exception to absolute prosecutorial immunity for chief and supervising advocates conflicts with the Supreme Court\u2019s precedent in Imbler v. Pachtman and its progeny."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Coates",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6ab8ec21006ec8570d912efa69199859f3cbda0c74cea37ba4b0609d14a02c90",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6ab8ec21006e-0002-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Coates, petitioners contend that the constitutional claim at issue concerns violations of the Giglio and Brady disclosure obligations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Coates",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6ab8ec21006ec8570d912efa69199859f3cbda0c74cea37ba4b0609d14a02c90",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6ab8ec21006e-0002-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Coates, petitioners assert that negligence in maintaining an administrative data system can cause constitutional violations, and that the presence of such a system could have prevented the misconduct at trial."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6ab8ec21006ec8570d912efa69199859f3cbda0c74cea37ba4b0609d14a02c90",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6ab8ec21006e-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, respondents argue that extending liability to supervisory prosecutors would expose them to suits and create anomalies that do not affect line prosecutors."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6ab8ec21006ec8570d912efa69199859f3cbda0c74cea37ba4b0609d14a02c90",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6ab8ec21006e-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, respondents maintain that the case does not concern whether a chief district attorney can set trial\u2011strategy policies, and that granting immunity to the chief DA would not affect the outcome."
      }
    ],
